        {
          "id": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1",
          "title": "Question 26 to 35 are based on the following passage.",
          "presentation": "reading",
          "instructions": [],
          "stimulusBlocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The U. S. Department of Education is making efforts to ensure that all students have equal access to a quality education. Today it is "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-26"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " the launch of the Excellent Educators for All Initiative. The initiative will help states and school districts support great educators for the students who need them most. “All children are "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-27"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " to a high-quality education regardless of their race, zip code or family income. It is "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-28"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " important that we provide teachers and principals the support they need to help students reach their full "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-29"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " ” U. S. Secretary of Education Arne Duncan said. “Despite the excellent work and deep "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-30"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " of our nation’s teachers and principals, students in high-poverty, high-minority schools are unfairly treated across our country. We have to do better. Local leaders and educators will "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-31"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " their own creative solutions, but we must work together to "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-32"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " our focus on how to better recruit, support and "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-33"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " effective teachers and principals for all students, especially the kids who need them most.” Today’s announcement is another important step forward in improving access to a quality education, a "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-34"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " of President Obama’s year of action. Later today, Secretary Duncan will lead a round table discussion with principals and school teachers from across the country about the "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015063-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-35"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " of working in high-need schools and how to adopt promising practices for supporting great educators in these schools."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
